# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
mt5env/

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Patch artefacts. Applying a .patch on the box used to leave the patch
# file in the tree (`autosync-fix-2026-10-20.patch`); it is not an input.
*.patch

# Data (large CSVs – download on demand instead)
#
# NOTE: this rule does NOT cover data/GOLD_M1.csv or data/GOLD_M5.csv, which
# are already tracked (gitignore never applies to a tracked file). So
# `tools/pull_gold_m5.sh` overwrites a TRACKED file and leaves the tree dirty -
# which autosync reads as "hand-edits on the server" and refuses to deploy.
# That is exactly what froze deploys on 2026-10-24. Either commit the pull or
# `git checkout -- data/GOLD_M5.csv` afterwards (the pull script now says so),
# or untrack both files deliberately:
#     git rm --cached data/GOLD_M1.csv data/GOLD_M5.csv
# This line still stops any NEW csv from being added by accident.
data/*.csv

# Runtime logs / status files.
# The durable paper state is PUBLISHED by tools/autosync.sh as `data collection N`
# commits, so those three files must stay trackable per book. Everything else in
# logs/ (live_status, connection_status, system.jsonl, deploy/autosync logs,
# locks, KILL_SWITCH, quarantine) is machine-local and ignored.
# `logs/` (with the trailing slash) would ignore the directory itself and make
# every `!` negation below a no-op - it has to be `logs/*`.
logs/*
!logs/ledger.jsonl
!logs/daily_stats.json
!logs/paper_account.json
# Derived liveness heartbeat (age of each engine's live_status.json). Published
# so "is it running?" is answerable from a checkout; see tools/heartbeat.py.
!logs/heartbeat.json
btc/logs/*
!btc/logs/ledger.jsonl
!btc/logs/daily_stats.json
!btc/logs/paper_account.json
# logs/trades.jsonl is deliberately NOT published: run.py writes a SIGNAL row
# every loop (~11,500 rows / ~1.7 MB a day). tools/ledger_export.py distils the
# trade lifecycle into ledger.jsonl; the raw log stays on the box.

# Secrets / local config
.env
*.env
credentials*
.env.*
!.env.example
